Cached `GetType()` and replaced the variable division by a 16-entry shift table, since FIT base-type sizes are powers of two. This removes a repeated type lookup and the expensive runtime integer division while preserving exact truncation behavior.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();
    if (type != FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
    {
        static const FIT_UINT8 shifts[16] = {0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 0, 2, 3, 0, 1, 2, 0, 3, 3};
        return (FIT_UINT8)(values.size() >> shifts[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK]);
    }

    return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();
}
```